        new(2, "Silver", "Freestyle Leap", "Choose one Knight. It may land on any intermediate square along its L-shaped routes, and still jumps over pieces. Two-by-two diagonals are excluded.", "One chosen Knight can land partway through its L-shaped leaps."),
        new(3, "Gold", "The Doppelganger", "Choose a Knight and Bishop to exchange movement. Every 4 moves by either side, keep or swap both together, or choose a new pair, without spending a move. If either piece type disappears from your army, restore normal movement. Your opponent sees a different Gold buff in the HUD.", "Swap a Knight and Bishop's movement while hiding your real buff from the enemy."),
        new(4, "Gold", "Suicide Bomber", "Once per match, your original Queen explodes when captured. All non-King pieces in the surrounding 3x3 area die, including the capturer and allies. Promoted Queens do not explode.", "Your original Queen explodes once when captured, destroying nearby non-Kings."),
        new(5, "Diamond", "Flying Thunder God", "Your original Queen may teleport to any empty square as her move, if your King remains safe. Recharge after 5 of your turns; maximum 5 uses. Promoted Queens cannot teleport.", "Teleport your original Queen to empty squares. Five uses, with a recharge."),
        new(6, "Silver", "Noble Sacrifice", "A Pawn may capture an allied Pawn diagonally ahead and become Bloodthirsty. It can then move or capture into any of the three squares ahead, but cannot eat another allied Pawn.", "Sacrifice an allied Pawn to empower another Pawn's forward movement and captures."),
        new(7, "Silver", "Absolute Sniper", "A Bishop capturing an enemy non-Pawn from 4 or more squares away empowers its next diagonal capture: it automatically shoots without moving or confirmation. The shot spends your move. The charge expires after the next 4 moves by either side.", "Long Bishop captures charge an automatic ranged capture without moving."),
        new(8, "Silver", "Gambling Leads to Misery", "A Pawn capturing an enemy has a 25% chance of an immediate extra move with that Pawn. Maximum 3 extra moves per match.", "Pawn captures have a 25% chance to grant another move. Up to three bonuses."),
        new(9, "Silver", "Loot Box", "At combined move 25 and 50, a crate lands on a random square and captures its occupant. Kings are protected at 25, but not at 50. Collect it to place a Rook, then a Queen, in your half; enemies destroy your crates.", "Crates at combined moves 25 and 50 let you deploy a Rook, then a Queen."),
        new(10, "Gold", "Peace T-shirt", "Keep your King out of check for the first 14 combined moves. Recruit one enemy other than a King or Queen into your first three ranks. If those ranks are full, you may replace a Pawn there.", "Avoid early checks to recruit an enemy piece into your home territory."),
        new(11, "Gold", "Devolution of Pawn?", "All your Pawns can retreat one empty square. Retreating onto your back rank sacrifices the Pawn and leaves a mine. An enemy entering it dies and consumes the mine.", "Retreat Pawns onto your back rank to turn them into deadly mines."),
        new(12, "Gold", "Mobile Fortress", "A Rook can carry one allied Pawn from its surrounding 3x3 area. Unload into an empty 3x3 square from your next turn. A destroyed carrier parachutes its Pawn nearby; landing on the far rank promotes it. These actions spend no move.", "Carry a nearby Pawn inside a Rook, then unload or parachute it to safety."),
        new(13, "Gold", "Hiding King", "At the start, swap your King unconditionally with an ally on your back rank. Afterward, recharge every 10 combined moves. Both pieces must then be on your back rank and your King must end safe.", "Swap your King with a back-rank ally, with an opening swap and later recharges."),
        new(14, "Gold", "Gacha Banner", "Capture an enemy non-Pawn for 1 ticket. Spend 1 ticket to drop a random ally at most once per turn: Pawn 70%, Knight 10%, Bishop 10%, Rook 9%, Queen 1%. The drop cannot check the opposing King.", "Capture non-Pawns for tickets. Spend one to summon a random ally each turn."),
        new(15, "Diamond", "Substitute Ninjutsu", "On your first check, teleport your King to a safe empty home square and leave a decoy. The decoy moves like a King and transforms into the first enemy type it captures.", "Your first check teleports the King to safety and leaves a transforming decoy."),
        new(16, "Diamond", "The High-tech Era", "Your two initial Rooks keep normal movement and can capture over exactly one piece. Each cannon expires after 10 combined moves without firing.", "Your initial Rooks become cannons that can capture over one blocker."),
        new(17, "Diamond", "The Queen's Betrayal", "Gain an extra Queen on your third rank. After each combined move, her betrayal chance starts at 10% and rises by 5 percentage points. On betrayal, the opponent places her in their first three ranks.", "Gain a powerful extra Queen whose growing betrayal risk may turn her against you."),
        new(18, "Diamond", "The Definition of CHAOS", "After your 10th turn, the outermost files collapse and destroy their pieces without capture points. Five combined moves later the next pair collapses, leaving a 4x8 board.", "The board's outer files collapse in two stages. Keep your army away from the edges."),
        new(19, "Diamond", "RNG Fiesta", "At the start, transform all your pieces except Kings and Queens randomly into Pawns, Knights, Bishops or Rooks.", "Randomize your starting army, keeping only Kings and Queens unchanged."),
        new(20, "Diamond", "I-Frame Roll", "When checkmated, choose a safe empty square within the 5x5 area centered on your King. Spend no move; maximum 3 escapes per match.", "Escape checkmate by moving your King to nearby safety, up to three times."),
        new(21, "Legendary", "Ghost Army", "Your pieces can pass through allies but cannot share a destination. Enemies still block paths. Phasing cannot be used to check the opposing King.", "Your army can pass through allies, but phasing cannot deliver check."),
        new(22, "Legendary", "Plague Town", "An enemy capturing your piece becomes infected and dies after the next 4 combined moves. Kings are immune.", "Enemies that capture your pieces are infected and die after four combined moves."),
        new(23, "Legendary", "Customize Army", "Rearrange your army within your half for up to 2 minutes, then confirm. An unchanged formation refunds this buff as a random Gold buff.", "Arrange your army in your half. An unchanged formation refunds a random Gold buff."),
        new(24, "Legendary", "Pawn's Revolution", "Sacrifice every piece except your King, then fill every empty square in your half with Pawns.", "Trade every non-King for a half-board filled with Pawns."),
        new(25, "Legendary", "One Man Army", "Keep only your King, who can also move two squares orthogonally. A rifle shot is available immediately and recharges every 3 of your turns, without stacking. Aim for 15 seconds; a miss or King/Queen hit ends the shot. You can still make your normal move.", "Fight with only an empowered King and a rifle that recharges every three owner turns."),
        new(26, "Silver", "Every Man for Himself", "Capture a matching enemy type with each of Pawn, Knight, Bishop, Rook and Queen, and promote a Pawn once. Then promote 2 surviving Pawns to Queens, or place 1 Queen anywhere if fewer than 2 remain. Any draw becomes a loss.", "Complete capture and promotion quests for a Queen reward. Any draw becomes a loss."),
        new(27, "Silver", "Sac ur Queen!!!", "Replace your initial Queen with your choice of Rook, Bishop or Knight. After 10 of your turns, transform one ally other than a King or promoted Queen into a Queen.", "Trade your Queen for a smaller piece, then reclaim a Queen after ten owner turns."),
